{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Corrected stack pushed: Gerrit **1399** (9f26) + **1400** (4b9e). **1398 ABANDONED.**\n\n### 1398 was green and wrong — that is the headline\n\n1398 held **LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1** — fully submittable — with the converged-parent defect\nin it. The bot review and CI both passed a change that would have alerted on every\ninbound-mirrored sub-task in the store, every pass. It was caught only by a separate adversarial\nread of the diff. **Abandoned so it cannot be submitted**, with the reason recorded on the change.\n\nAlso worth recording: `git commit --amend` with `-F -` and a fresh message **drops the\n`Change-Id` trailer**, so the corrected commits minted NEW change numbers instead of a patchset\non 1398. That is what left a green-but-wrong change sitting there submittable. Preserve the\ntrailer (or amend with `--no-edit`) when correcting a pushed change.\n\n### Final gate results — real exit codes, not piped through tail\n\n| gate | exit | detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `make lint` | **0** | ruff check + format-check, zizmor, actionlint |\n| `make typecheck` | **0** | mypy, 432 source files |\n| `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 4 --dist worksteal -q` | **0** | **10202 passed, 38 skipped** |\n\nThe marker selection mattered: a `tests/unit` path subset would have MISSED\n`test_comment_hygiene_guard.py`, which failed my first attempt on a bare run-id citation in a\ndocstring. Docstrings now carry grouped-hex ticket ids alongside the run id.\n\n### Files in each change\n\n**1399 (9f26)** — 4 files:\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_field_diff.py` (+47/-…, the only production file) ·\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_parent_emit_suppression_is_loud_9f26.py` (new, 9 cells) ·\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py` (2 cells re-homed + probes re-homed to the\nrefusal cell) · `docs/jira-dc-capability-map.md` (+32)\n\n**1400 (4b9e)** — 1 file, test-only:\n`tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py` (`test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips`\nre-homed to the Epic Link, primed through a local rebar edit so the ref is MANAGED)\n\n### Scope discipline held\n\n`set_parent` lives in `_hierarchy.py`, **not** `transport.py` — so the `_paged_search` region\nanother agent owns (ticket 18a4) was never touched. Nothing under `.github/workflows/` or\n`scripts/` was touched either. The production diff is confined to one function and its single\ncaller in one file.\n\n### Still NOT closing this ticket\n\nThe three cells run only in the live harness. AC4/AC5 need a harness run to verify, and the\nVerified +1 policy says do not close before the change lands. Handing back for verification."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785889843307368001,"uuid":"f2f4c03f-aa7e-4975-ad7a-fec90b694f59"}